{"author":{"id":"8044233cc21d4498a49e4a5a452ed824a81830d46e1fdc556b7dd44b12149dae"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1534593058,"nonce":"BsAOvfpRSrSZ3XfXDajrquqOFk4=","metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQxNDA1MjYxOQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/git-bug/git-bug/issues/18#issuecomment-414052619"},"message":"We can't have numbers (see https://github.com/MichaelMure/git-bug/blob/master/doc/model.md#you-cant-have-a-simple-consecutive-index-for-your-bugs) but we can use the shorter hash.\n\nThe tricky part is that git-bug is entirely decoupled from the normal code workflow (by design). Having this kind of feature would require git-bug to track changes in the normal branches and edit bugs accordingly.\n\nMaybe git-bug could install a hook to spy on the normal workflow and trigger these changes ? The problem is that every single commiter of the repo would need to have git-bug installed or some of these events would be missed.","files":null}]}